    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d4-f1" n="1" xml:id="d4-f1-content">
                <p>The Second Special Session of the General Assembly, meeting at New York, April
                    16–May 14, 1948, was convened to consider the Palestine problem. Also, it was at
                    this time (April 19) that the Union of Burma was admitted to membership in the
                    United Nations Organization.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d4-f2" n="2" xml:id="d4-f2-content">
                <p>John C. Ross was Deputy to the United States Representative at the United
                    Nations. This position is not to be confused with that of Deputy United States
                    Representative at the United Nations, which at this time had not yet been
                    established.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d4-f3" n="3" xml:id="d4-f3-content">
                <p>Dean Rusk was Director of the Office of United Nations Affairs, Department of
                    State.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d4-f4" n="4" xml:id="d4-f4-content">
                <p>The Advisory Staff were officers of the Department of State unless otherwise
                    designated.</p>
            </note>
